`crates/mail-core/src/gmail/provider.rs` — `pace()`:

- Reservation under the existing `last_request_slot` mutex changed from
  `previous + interval` to `(previous + interval).max(Instant::now())`
  (`None` slot reserves `Instant::now()`, unchanged). Idle periods and slow
  responses can no longer accumulate past-due slots that let consecutive
  reads burst until the schedule "catches up".
- Doc comment updated to state the rebase constraint.

New regression test `overdue_slots_rebase_to_now_instead_of_granting_burst_credit`
(provider unit tests, offline, loopback fake API):

- Seeds `last_request_slot` with `Instant::now() - 3600s` (via `checked_sub`),
  sets `min_request_interval = 150ms`, then performs two `list_inbox` reads.
